  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f8bc3154-e9da-5291-a9a4-49ecd35c323a" activityNameId="5b11f2d4-9b09-5c42-966e-bfd3200685ca" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Copper, primary, at refinery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Copper, primary, at refinery
The product "copper, primary, at refinery" is used as pure metal or as alloying element in various technical applications.;
CAS number: 007440-50-8; 
UUID: 987dc6b3-6f8a-3736-8969-047831fe190f
The module includes the pre-treatment of the ore, the reduction and the refining copper to cathode copper, including the country-specific share in hydrometalurgically won copper (SX-EW)
Location: This module is valid for the whole corresponding region. Some agents used like lime or sodium cyanide originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe.
Technology: The ore is pre-treated,  reduced and refined according to the country specific mix of process alternatives: reverberatory furnace 6.2%; flash smelting furnaces 76.0%; other 17.8%.; SX-EW 0.0%. An overall abatement for sulphur dioxide of 95.0% was estimated.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 9.5 million tonnes in Cu in 1994
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_987dc6b3-6f8a-3736-8969-047831fe190f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">RER</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: This module is valid for the whole corresponding region. Some agents used like lime or sodium cyanide originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe.</text>
        </comment>
      </geography>
      <technology>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Technology: The ore is pre-treated,  reduced and refined according to the country specific mix of process alternatives: reverberatory furnace 6.2%; flash smelting furnaces 76.0%; other 17.8%.; SX-EW 0.0%. An overall abatement for sulphur dioxide of 95.0% was estimated.</text>
        </comment>
      </technology>
